# changes.ges — the zero change at a type, decided in the language
#
# `card:types-in-the-host.md`, shape (c) — Henri, 2026-09-16: *"yea. it
# all seems ok."*  The compiler's change structure (`spec/data.md`
# §I.4.2, §I.4.3) says what the zero change at each type is.  Until
# today that decision was a `case` over the compiler's own types in
# `gestate/changes.py`, where the checker could not see it.  Now the
# **decision** is here, over a `Type` value the compiler reads back from
# an inferred type (`stage.reflect`), and the host builds the expression
# the shape says — a `()`, a `⊥`, a pair, a `dummy`, a lambda.
#
# Compiled after `facts.ges`, which holds `Type`.  This file has no
# `fix` and no set in it, on purpose: the transform that asks for zero
# changes runs only over a program that uses one, so it never asks while
# this file is being compiled (Q3 of the card).

#: The shape of a zero change: nothing (`ΔInt = 1`, and every discrete
#: type), the empty set (`Δ{A} = {A}`), the pair of the components'
#: shapes (`Δ(A×B) = ΔA × ΔB`), a `dummy` of the value at a type with
#: constructors (`Δ(A+B)`: the tag is the value's, so the host needs it),
#: and a function's — the shape of its result (`Δ(A→B) = □A → ΔA → ΔB`).
Zero := ZUnit | ZBottom | ZPair (List Zero) | ZDummy | ZFun Zero

#: The zero change at a type, given the names of the types that have
#: constructors.  A tuple is componentwise; a function's is its
#: result's; a set is `⊥`; a type somebody declared is a `dummy`; and
#: everything else — `Int`, `Char`, `Cyclic n`, `lo .. hi`, `□A`, every
#: Rizzo former — is discrete, so its change is nothing.
zeroShape : List Text -> Type -> Zero
zeroShape adts t = case t of
    TyTuple parts -> ZPair (map (zeroShape adts) parts)
    TyFun a r -> ZFun (zeroShape adts r)
    TyInt n -> ZUnit
    other -> case typeHead t == "Set" of
        True -> ZBottom
        False -> case elem (typeHead t) adts of
            True -> ZDummy
            False -> ZUnit

#: The name at the head of a type — `Set` of `Set (Int, Text)`, `Int`
#: of `Int`; a type-level number has none.
typeHead : Type -> Text
typeHead t = case t of
    TyApp f a -> typeHead f
    TyCon n -> n
    other -> ""
